      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) given that \\(\\tan x = 2\\), we can use the tangent addition formula. The formula for the tangent of a sum of two angles is:\n\n\\[\n\\tan (a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}\n\\]\n\nIn this problem, we have \\(a = x\\) and \\(b = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\). We know that \\(\\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = 1\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\tan x = 2\\) and \\(\\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = 1\\), we substitute these values into the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) is \\(\\boxed{-3}\\).",
