      "text": "We are given that $\\tan x = 2$. We need to find $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)$. Using the tangent addition formula, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\n\\]\nSince $\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1$, the formula simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]\nTo verify our solution using Python, we can perform the calculation directly. Let's write the Python code to confirm the result.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Given value\ntan_x = 2\n\n# Calculate tan(x + pi/4) using the tangent addition formula\ntan_pi_over_4 = 1\nresult = (tan_x + tan_pi_over_4) / (1 - tan_x * tan_pi_over_4)\n\nprint(result)\n```",
